            "Another challenging type of mistake is caused by over-splitting. In the following example, as a result of decomposition, the information of ``{\\it after}'' is lost. In this case, a candidate of correct decomposition is not to decompose the latter two sentences as ``{\\it Shine Limited was set up by former BSkyB executive Elisabeth Murdoch {\\bf after} she quit as broadcaster}''.\n",
